( 9. Nfxd4?! {The other knight has somewhere better to be.} ) ) ( 3... d6
{The Steinitz. Solid, passive, and it hands White a check. [%weight 3]} 4. Bxc6+
{With check, so Black cannot choose the recapture. [%tags doubled-pawns]} 4... bxc6
{Forced. [%weight 9]} 5. d4
{The centre at once, as in the 4...bxc6 chapter. [%tags d4-break]} ( 5. O-O!?
{Also fine and a shade slower. With a pawn on d6 the break is the right first move.} )
5... exd4 {Black takes. [%weight 6]} 6. Qxd4 {The queen, with no knight to chase her.}
6... Be7 {Black develops. [%weight 6]} 7. Nc3 {Everything out.} 7... Nf6
{Black develops. [%weight 6]} 8. Bf4
{Hitting d6 and taking the dark squares. [%tags bishop-placement]} ( 8. Bg5?!
{It pins nothing useful and invites ...h6 with tempo. On f4 it hits the pawn on d6.} )
8... O-O {Black castles. [%weight 6]} 9. O-O-O
{Towards the weak pawns, and the rook lands on the file Black has to watch. [%tags king-safety] [%plan Play Rhe1 and e5, or h4 and h5. Pawns on a6, c6 and c7 cannot be defended by other pawns.] [%line The Steinitz, 3...d6]}
( 9. O-O?! {It castles away from the play.} ) ) ( 3... f5
{The Schliemann. Black hits e4 and lets the bishop take. [%weight 2]} 4. Bxc6
{Take first, which removes the defender of e5 as well. [%tags doubled-pawns]} 4... dxc6
{Towards the centre. [%weight 7]} 5. Nc3
{Defend the pawn with a piece and develop in the same move.} ( 5. Nxe5?!
{It grabs and gives it back with interest: Black takes on e4 with a free centre and lines at the king.}
) 5... fxe4 {Black resolves it. [%weight 7]} 6. Nxe4 {The knight lands in the middle.}
6... Nf6 {Black challenges it. [%weight 6]} 7. Qe2
{Holding the knight and eyeing the file Black opened himself. [%plan Play d3 and Bg5, castle, and use the open e-file against a king that has not moved.] [%line The Schliemann, 3...f5]}
( 7. Nxf6+?!
{It relieves the pressure and develops Black. Keep the knight and let Black do the trading.}
) ) ( 3... g6 {The fianchetto. Slow and playable. [%weight 2]} 4. Bxc6
{Take. [%tags doubled-pawns]} 4... dxc6 {Towards the centre. [%weight 7]} 5. d3
{Quiet. The pawn on e4 is held and the position stays closed for the bishop that is coming to g7.}
( 5. d4?! {It opens the diagonal for the bishop about to arrive on g7. Keep it shut.} )
5... Bg7 {Black finishes the fianchetto. [%weight 8]} 6. Nbd2
{The knight heads for c4. [%cal Gd2c4]} 6... Ne7 {Black develops towards g6. [%weight 6]}
7. Nc4 {It arrives, eyeing e5 and b6.} 7... O-O {Black castles. [%weight 7]} 8. Ncxe5
{Count before you take, and the count says take: the pawn is attacked twice and defended once. [%tags tactics] [%cal Gc4e5,Gf3e5]}
